Algorithm: Medical Diagnosis Using Backward Chaining

Step 1: Start the program.

Step 2: Define the patient's symptoms:

Fever
Cough
Headache
Body pain
Sore throat

Step 3: Define the disease rules:

Fever + cough + body pain → Flu
Cough + sore throat → Cold
Fever + headache + body pain → Malaria

Step 4: Start the diagnosis with the goal diagnose(Disease).

Step 5: Prolog checks the rule:
diagnose(Disease) :- disease(Disease).

Step 6: Prolog tries to prove disease(Disease) by checking each disease rule.

Step 7: For each disease, check whether all required symptoms are available.

Step 8: If all symptoms required by a rule are true, conclude that the disease is a possible diagnosis.

Step 9: Continue checking other disease rules to find all possible diagnoses.

Step 10: Display the possible diseases and stop when no more solutions are found.
